      "description": "Watch Hapoel Beer Sheva vs Dinamo Zagreb highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 16, 2026. The stage was set for a compelling UEFA Europa League encounter as Hapoel Be’er Sheva hosted Dinamo Zagreb in a match characterized by tactical discipline and high-stakes maneuvering. Both sides looked to establish their dominance early in the group stage, leading to a fiercely contested battle. Early Setbacks and Tactical Adjustments Kicking off on September 16, 2026 , the match began with a high tempo as both teams vied for control of the midfield. The visitors, Dinamo Zagreb , faced an early challenge when Lukas Kacavenda was forced off in the 24th minute. Miha Zajc was called upon to fill the void, shifting the tactical balance of the opening period. Despite the disruption, both defenses remained organized, neutralizing potential threats and heading into the halftime break with everything still to play for. A Flurry of Changes in the Second Half As the second half got underway, the managerial chess match intensified. In the 64th minute, Dinamo Zagreb opted for a double substitution, bringing on Luka Ivanusec and Smail Prevljak for Mislav Orsic and Arber Hoxha . Not to be outdone, Hapoel Be’er Sheva introduced Amir Ganah shortly after to spark their attacking line. The substitutions continued to flow as Javon East and Forson Amankwah made way for Mohammed Abu Rumi and Mohamad Kanaan in the 75th minute. In a desperate bid to find a breakthrough, both managers utilized their benches extensively in the closing stages. Iker Almena and Kirill Kravtsov joined the action for Dinamo , while Hapoel shored up their defensive options with Idan Nachmias and Ofir Davidzada entering in the 83rd minute. The referee eventually blew the final whistle after four minutes of stoppage time, concluding a night where tactical rigidity triumphed over attacking flair."
